From: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: manage virtual port and netdevice lifetime

A virtual port is a PPE port number past the physical ones, bound to a net
device the PPE cannot reach directly - a wireless VAP. It lets the L3 flow
engine forward to such a device: the flow is forwarded to the virtual port,
whose L2_VP_PORT_TBL entry points its physical port at the CPU and its
unicast queue at the CPU port's queue, so the packet is delivered to the
host on an EDMA ring already rewritten, to be transmitted out the device.

Register a net device notifier for the virtual ports. When a bound device
unregisters, force its virtual port down and clear the registry so the
receive path drops the stale pointer before the device is freed; any flows
still referencing the port release it harmlessly once they are torn down.
When a bound device's link changes, update the flowtable carrier so a flow
to a down device stops refreshing its conntrack, the same stuck-flow guard
the physical ports use.

Merged from:
  0517-01-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-add-virtual-ports.patch
  0517-02-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-track-virtual-port-device-events.patch

Based on work by:
  Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>

Signed-off-by: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/Makefile
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_QCOM_PPE) += qcom-ppe.o
-qcom-ppe-objs := ppe.o ppe_config.o ppe_debugfs.o ppe_port.o ppe_api.o ppe_bridge.o ppe_flow.o ppe_flowtable.o
+qcom-ppe-objs := ppe.o ppe_config.o ppe_debugfs.o ppe_port.o ppe_api.o ppe_bridge.o ppe_flow.o ppe_flowtable.o ppe_vp.o
 qcom-ppe-objs += ppe_tunnel.o
 
 #EDMA
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include "ppe_flow.h"
 #include "ppe_tunnel.h"
 #include "ppe_flowtable.h"
+#include "ppe_vp.h"
 #include "ppe_port.h"
 
 #define PPE_PORT_MAX		8
@@ -283,6 +284,16 @@ static int qcom_ppe_probe(struct platfor
 				     "PPE flowtable offload setup failed\n");
 	}
 
+	ret = ppe_vp_setup(ppe_dev);
+	if (ret) {
+		ppe_port_mac_deinit(ppe_dev);
+		ppe_flowtable_destroy(ppe_dev);
+		ppe_bridge_destroy(ppe_dev);
+		edma_destroy(ppe_dev);
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "PPE virtual port setup failed\n");
+	}
+
 	ppe_debugfs_setup(ppe_dev);
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, ppe_dev);
 
@@ -301,6 +312,7 @@ static void qcom_ppe_remove(struct platf
 	 * ports still exist.
 	 */
 	ppe_flowtable_destroy(ppe_dev);
+	ppe_vp_teardown(ppe_dev);
 	ppe_bridge_destroy(ppe_dev);
 	ppe_debugfs_teardown(ppe_dev);
 	edma_destroy(ppe_dev);
